# HW10 Reproducible Run Instructions

Run all commands from the `data260-4544/` project root.

## Install dependencies

```bash
python -m pip install -r code/requirements-hw08.txt
```

## Start the local judge model

Make sure Ollama is running and the documented model is installed:

```bash
ollama serve
ollama pull qwen2.5:3b
```

## Run Part 2 - Automated evaluation

```bash
python code/hw10_evaluate.py
```

This saves `evaluation_results.json` and appends the result to `RUN_LOG.txt`.

## Run Part 3 - Judge validation

The frozen `eval_cases.json` and `human_labels.csv` must not be changed after
the judge run begins.

```bash
python code/hw10_evaluate.py --validate-judge
```

This runs the same 20 cases three times and saves `judge_runs.json` and
`judge_validation.json`.

## Run Part 4 - Tracing and latency analysis

```bash
python code/hw10_evaluate.py --tracing
```

This saves `traces.jsonl`, `latency_results.csv`, and `metrics.json`, and
appends the trace and latency evidence to `RUN_LOG.txt`.

## Run the HW10 verification script

```bash
python code/verify-hw10.py
```

The verifier writes `reports/hw10/verification.json`.

## Open the dashboard

```bash
streamlit run code/hw10_dashboard.py
```

